  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Education obligated $2.2B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency recorded 669 awards with an average award size of $3.2M, and obligations fell 13.6% year over year. Yearly obligations have moved between $2.4B and $2.7B since FY22, with FY21 at $2.7B, FY22 at $2.4B, FY23 at $2.4B, FY24 at $2.7B, and FY25 at $2.5B. Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation is the largest spending category at $935M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $663M. Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities accounts for $149M of obligations, while multiple IT and services categories together make up significant remaining spending. ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC is the top vendor at $340M, followed by NELNET SERVICING LLC at $294M and MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC at $251M. The mix shows strong emphasis on credit intermediation, IT systems, and social science research in the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What drove Education's contract spending this year?",
        "body": "Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation drove the largest share of obligations at $935M. Computer Systems Design Services also drove a major portion of spending at $663M. Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities contributed $149M, with several other IT and financial services categories adding smaller but meaningful amounts."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries dominate Education contracting?",
        "body": "ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC is the largest vendor at $340M, followed by NELNET SERVICING LLC at $294M and MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC at $251M. The top categories are concentrated in credit intermediation and IT services, with Computer Systems Design Services at $663M and Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation at $935M. A mix of loan servicers and research contractors appears among the highest-ranked vendors and NAICS categories."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Education spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Education obligated $2.2B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency recorded 669 awards with an average award size of $3.2M, and obligations fell 13.6% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations ranged from $2.4B to $2.7B in recent years, with FY21 at $2.7B and FY25 at $2.5B."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Education buy?",
      "a": "Education buys services concentrated in Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation and Computer Systems Design Services. Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation accounts for $935M and Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $663M, with Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities at $149M and several IT-related services making up the rest."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Education's largest contractors?",
      "a": "ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC is the largest contractor at $340M. NELNET SERVICING LLC follows at $294M, MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC at $251M, EDFINANCIAL SERVICES LLC at $193M, and MAXIMUS FEDERAL SERVICES, INC. at $158M, with other top vendors including MISSOURI HIGHER EDUCATION LOAN AUTHORITY at $140M and CENTRAL RESEARCH INC at $70.2M."
